# Trivy baseline for Studafy CI.
#
# These findings pre-date the trivy version pin (see .github/workflows/containers.yml and
# ci.yml, pinned to trivy-action@0.36.0 / trivy v0.72.0). They were introduced by upstream
# check/CVE-database growth in `trivy-action@master`, not by any application change, and were green
# when the corresponding infrastructure originally merged. Each entry is a deliberate, documented
# waiver -- revisit when the underlying resource or base image is next changed.
#
# QA-073: every waiver needs a `# review-by: YYYY-MM-DD` line in the comment block directly above
# its ID. scripts/ci/check-trivyignore-expiry.sh (ci.yml's quality job) fails on or after that
# date: remove the waiver if the finding is fixed, or re-justify it with a new date.
#
# NOTE: trivy .trivyignore does not support trailing inline comments; IDs must be bare on their own
# line. Keep the explanatory notes as full-line comments above each ID.

# --- Container images ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No image CVEs are waived here. The app-owned images are scanned strictly (exit-code 1). The
# erpnext image rides the unmodified third-party frappe/erpnext base whose CVE set churns with
# trivy's DB, so its scan is report-only via the trivy_exit_code matrix field in containers.yml
# rather than an unmaintainable per-CVE allowlist here.

# --- JS/TS dependencies (bun.lock), found by ci.yml's security-scan job's vuln scanner ------------
# QA-073 removed four waivers that no longer matched anything: brace-expansion (CVE-2026-14257,
# CVE-2026-69152) is now at 1.1.21 / 2.1.7 / 5.0.12, and nanoid (CVE-2026-67213, CVE-2026-67214) at
# 3.3.19, all past their fixed versions.

# tmp@0.1.0 (via @lhci/cli@0.15.1, pulled by apps/web's perf:lighthouse budget run) -- path
# traversal via unsanitized prefix/postfix. Fixed at 0.2.6, but @lhci/cli 0.15.1 declares
# `tmp: ^0.1.0`, and forcing it needs an unsafe flat override (tmp also has dependents on
# incompatible scopes here: exceljs wants ^0.2.x, already resolved past the fix at 0.2.7;
# external-editor wants ^0.0.33 and needs that exact API). LHCI runs Lighthouse inside CI only --
# it is dev tooling, never shipped to production. @lhci/cli 0.16.1 (2026-11-11) drops tmp; it is
# held back only by the 7-day Dependabot cooldown, so bump it and delete this waiver.
# review-by: 2027-01-15
CVE-2026-44705
